::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: rule-namespaced fixture ]

Three layers and one edge that runs the wrong way, with the rule written
in its namespaced spelling.

==[ crate-layering ]

Every workspace member belongs to exactly one layer, and depends only on
layers strictly below its own.

@writ.rule(crate-layering){
  guard: { twrit: layers }

  layers: {
    2: list("top")
    1: list("mid")
    0: list("base")
  }
}

`mid` depends on `top`, which is one layer up. That single edge is what
this fixture exists to produce.

`base` is the floor and depends on nothing, so the floor rule stays out
of the way and only the upward edge is reported.
